<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sayyid dynasty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sayyid dynasty ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> in the first half of the fifteenth century, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sack-of-delhi-1398">sack of Delhi</a> in 1398. Its founder, Khizr Khan, had served as a Timurid governor. Accounts of the Delhi Sultanate describe the Sayyids as governing as Timurid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> over a much reduced state before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi dynasty</a> replaced them.</p></div>
